Third-party files
=================

The Join Order Benchmark (V. Leis, A. Gubichev, A. Mirchev, P. Boncz,
A. Kemper and T. Neumann, "How Good Are Query Optimizers, Really?", PVLDB
9(3), 2015): the SQL files of queries/job_all/ and queries/job_kept/ are its
113 queries, renamed (17b.sql is q17_b.sql) and otherwise unchanged, and
sql/job_schema.sql and sql/job_fkindexes.sql are its schema and foreign-key
indexes, all copied by scripts/job_queries.py from
https://github.com/gregrahn/join-order-benchmark at commit
a39603662e023e449cb2121997a5034df9e02ebf (queries/job_all/source.json holds
the SHA-256 of every copied file). That repository states no license; these
files keep their authors' terms and are not covered by the licenses above.
The IMDB data the queries run on are not part of this repository:
scripts/load_job.sh downloads the benchmark authors' snapshot, which comes
from IMDb and is subject to IMDb's terms of use.

project.sty and watml.sty are the course's style files and keep their
authors' terms.
